// Boxes pushed apart because they would otherwise overlap.
//
// Nothing here says that the wide box must clear "left" — that is implicit on
// every pair. What the file does say is enough to fix the direction: "middle"
// is right of "left", and the wide box is centered under "middle", so the file
// lets the wide box travel rightward away from "left" and offers no way back.
// Separating the other way would contradict a line that was written.
//
// The wide box also sits below "left", so both axes could separate the pair.
// The tie goes to whichever they overlap less. "left" is tall, so they share a
// lot of vertical space and very little horizontal, and the sideways push wins.
//
// The benchmark does not exercise any of this, so this file is the coverage.

box left    "L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L"
box right   "R"                             right of left
box middle  "m"   right of left  left of right  level with left
box wide    "a wide box that overruns both"    below middle  gap: tight
